From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:41:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: unblock_task refuses a stale copy of a done
 card; terminal-guard review nits

PR #1958 review 5889419180. 'unblocked' is an explicit reopen in kanban_terminal_guard and on the
Board (hermes-hub#105), but unblock_task's automated callers (shared-blocker clear and probe
election, quota release, resolved_check) act on the local row and never consulted terminal_hold:
on a stale blocked/scheduled copy of a done card they wrote 'unblocked', set the row ready, and
the push carried that to the Board as a reopen.

- unblock_task: kanban_terminal_guard.unblock_held refuses a held card inside the write txn,
  before precondition and the reason comment's savepoint, leaving one stale_wake_ignored note
  (producer:unblocked). Live cards (never completed, or completed then reopened) unblock as before.
- nit 2: comment why _restore_held compares local ids (arrival order).
- nit 3: enforce_after_apply drops the dead 'or was' fallback.
- reopen_review_task moves to kanban_db_review_reopen (re-exported) to keep kanban_db under its
  FILE_LINES cap.

Proof: the 4 new tests in test_kanban_stale_wake_terminal.py fail 3 on the PR head (unblock
returns True, row ready, precondition ran) and pass with the fix; mutants (status filter dropped,
check moved inside the comment savepoint) are killed.
